// Caddy Coach drill library: practice drills tied to the swing faults the analysis finds. Each has its coaching (what it
// fixes, why, kit, setup, steps, feel, mistakes, practice, success checks, progression) and a choreographed 3D demo.
// Coaching fields: aim (one line for the card), cue (one external focus, shown on the page and spoken in live
// feedback), test ({q, of, pass}: a scored test, two passes in a row move the golfer to the next progress step), cat (setup/grip/backswing/transition/downswing/impact/finish), level
// (1 beginner, 2 intermediate, 3 advanced), fault, why, kit, kitAlt, setup, steps + feel (one per step), sense, mistakes
// ([mistake, fix] pairs), dose (short), rx (the practice plan), success, progress, note (where golfers differ).
// No drill names a player or coach as using it, and no drill quotes a statistic it can't back up.
// Choreography: seq = keyframes {k: pose, o: overrides, d: seconds to get there, hold, step: which written step it shows,
// cam: view, cut: jump straight to this key's view, pace: 'slow' | 'real' | 'hold' | a word (a chip on the picture),
// lab: labels pinned to the body [{at, text, tone, side}], arr: arrows, ln: reference lines (spine, shoulders, plumb),
// hl: body parts to glow, ghost: a red "not this" pose, badge: big tick/cross, say: big word (counts),
// trail: draw the clubhead path, hit: ball goes (bag: it hits an impact bag instead), noball: no ball at this key}.
