    fault: 'Coming over the top: in the downswing the hands and club move out toward the ball first, so the club cuts across the ball from outside.',
    why: 'An over-the-top path starts the ball left of target and spins it right (for a right-hander): pulls and slices. The angled stick gives you a physical plane to swing under, so you feel the club dropping behind you before it moves out to the ball.',
    kitAlt: 'No alignment stick? An old shaft or a long garden cane works. Never use anything you would mind being hit.',
    setup: 'Push one end of the stick into the ground on the far side of the ball, then angle it up and back so it rises over the target line behind the ball, at about hand height. A good downswing passes underneath it; an over-the-top one runs into it.',
    steps: ['Push a stick into the ground beyond the ball and angle it up and back over the line behind the ball.',
      'Make slow swings, feeling the hands and club drop down under the stick on the way down.',
      'If the club or your hands hit the stick, you came over the top.',
      'Hit balls with slow, then normal swings, still under the stick.',
      'After 10 to 15 minutes, take the stick away and copy the feeling.'],
    feel: ['A ramp angled over the ball.', 'The hands dropping behind you first.', 'An honest touch tells you.', 'Swinging out toward the target from the inside.', 'The same drop without the stick.'],
    sense: 'At the start of the downswing, your hands dropping down behind you toward your trail hip, so the club approaches the ball from inside, under the stick, rather than out over it.',
    mistakes: [['Setting the stick so low you can\'t avoid it.', 'It should sit above a good swing. Check with slow swings first.'],
      ['Swinging under it by dropping the whole body.', 'Keep your posture; let the arms and club drop, not your head.'],
      ['Swinging fast straight away.', 'Start at half speed. A fast swing into a stick can damage it or the club.']],
    rx: 'Slow rehearsals for 5 minutes, then 10 to 15 minutes of shots at three-quarter effort. Finish with 5 balls without the stick.',
    success: ['You can make three-quarter swings without touching the stick.', 'Divots point at or slightly right of the target (for a right-hander) rather than left.', 'Slices curve less or start right and come back.'],
    progress: ['Slow swings under the stick, no ball.', 'Half shots.', 'Three-quarter and full shots.', 'Without the stick, checking the path on video down the line.'],
    note: 'Swing planes differ: some good players come down steeper than others and still hit it well. The stick catches an outside-in path, not a steep one with a good path.',
    view: 'dtl', camo: { dist: 4.6, ty: 0.85 }, scene: 'range', ball: true, poster: 3,
